    "body": "The three `Slow` cases in Test_Statics_Properties.re counted how often a property held and printed a distribution. None of them asserted, so a regression in any of the three was invisible.\r\n\r\nEach is now a real QCheck property wrapped in the `Alcotest.skip()` shape already used for `Preservation of types (disabled)` in Test_Evaluator_Properties.re, so the code stays compiled and re-enabling is a one-line edit.\r\n\r\nAll three properties are false. `Elaboration preserves type` was the surprise: its survey reported 1000/1000, but the survey seeded `Random.State.make([|0xC0FFEE|])`, and QCHECK_SEED=1 fails. The other two shrink to `(()) +. - []` (parent Float, fresh Int) and `{}`.\r\n\r\nDropped with the survey loops: two hand-rolled shrinkers that duplicated each other and QCheck's own shrinking, the outcome variants the loops tallied, and `show_exp`, which was a verbatim copy of QCheck_Util.show_core_exp.\r\n\r\n`show_core_typ` moves out of `arb_typ` to a top-level let beside `show_core_exp`. Typ.show prints the whole IdTagged record, which rendered a type disagreement as two ten-line blobs rather than Float vs Int.",
    "created_at": "2026-09-10T19:14:57Z",
